  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and economic development through support to local enterprise</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centro de Desenvolvimento Comunitario (CDC) seeks to contribute to the process of making the country&#x2019;s economy more self-sufficient and less dependent on imported goods, through promotion of food security, resource sovereignty and sustainable livelihoods for Timorese people living in peri-urban and rural areas.  Training and technical support are given to a range of community-based producer groups and service providers, and small entrepreneurs, always in response to their own request.  Target beneficiaries are often, but not always, engaged in food production or post-harvest processing of foodstuffs.  Capacity-building is provided in bookkeeping and other record maintenance, business plans, trade skills, marketing and sourcing of inputs/ raw materials, co-operative working etc.  Recycling is encouraged, to reduce the need for imports, and research is carried out into traditional skills and tools, resource requirements, opportunities for diversification.  A particular challenge which the project seeks to address is the difficulty faced by local producers in East Timor in competing with imported products, which are often cheaper.</narrative>
  </description>
